# building ermine

needs: deno 2.9.7 (what CI pins), a C11 compiler (cc), make. macOS's leaks for `make test-leaks`.

## checks

    deno lint                 lint (deno.json: what is excluded)
    deno fmt --check          formatting; deno fmt to fix
    deno task check           types

## TypeScript

    make test                 every TypeScript test, each with only the permissions it needs, then
                              every conformance suite against the TypeScript harnesses (what CI runs)
    deno task conformance [suite...] [--c | --check | --leaks]
                              the conformance suites alone; --c against the C harnesses, --check
                              against their sanitizer builds, --leaks under leaks

## C

    make                      every harness
    make check                every harness-check: address and undefined-behaviour sanitizers
    make test-c               each conformance suite against its C harness
    make test-check           the same against the harness-checks
    make test-leaks           the same under macOS's leaks
    WERROR=1                  with any of these: the harnesses' warnings are errors (CI builds so)
    <package>/c/build.sh      one package's harnesses alone; CHECK=1: its harness-checks

## measuring

    deno task perf [--c]      how cost grows with size
    deno task bench           deno's benches
    make bench                the C benches

## packaging

    deno publish --dry-run    what each workspace package would publish to JSR

